ecutor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor blacklisted usb-storage via modprobe.d (blacklist + install /bin/false) and rebuilt initramfs, directly verifying modprobe refuses to load the module both before and after a genuine, independently-verified reboot (boot_id changed from 242af11e... to ba406a82..., corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots). Both material outcomes of the task — blocking the module now and after reboot — are satisfied with direct evidence, and the mandatory restart evidence protocol was executed cleanly with no unnecessary mutations or residue.\",\"limitations\":[\"The restart evidence protocol only directly re-checked module-load blocking after reboot; broader 'service/data/cluster state' recovery was represented only by failed-services and package-health checks, which is reasonable for a single-node, non-clustered task but leaves no deeper application-level recovery evidence.\",\"Connectivity loss during reboot (cmd-9e8cc23db5d544c4) was a single timed-out probe rather than a full poll loop capture, though it is consistent with an in-progress reboot and the return code was not treated as a failure.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"block-now","requirement":"usb-storage kernel module is prevented from loading immediately (now)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Blacklist config with 'blacklist usb-storage' and 'install usb-storage /bin/false' was written to /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-usb-storage.conf, and modprobe usb-storage was directly observed to fail with 'could not insert usb_storage: Invalid argument' immediately after applying the config, with the module confirmed absent from lsmod.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0fc0c848f46044c6"]},{"id":"block-persistent","requirement":"usb-storage kernel module is prevented from loading after a reboot (persistence across restart)","status":"satisfied","summary":"A genuine reboot was performed and directly observed: pre-restart boot_id 242af11e... was captured with a he